<abstract>
<para>
&i18n-kapplication; is a client apps for RocketChat.
</para>
</abstract>

<keywordset>
<keyword>KDE</keyword>
<keyword>RocketChat</keyword>
</keywordset>
</bookinfo>

<chapter id="introduction">
<title>Introduction</title>
<para>&i18n-kapplication; is a desktop client for Rocket.Chat servers. It lets you
chat in channels, private groups, discussions and teams, exchange direct messages,
share files, and administer a server, all from a native &kde; application.</para>

<para>&i18n-kapplication; can be connected to several Rocket.Chat servers at the
same time and lets you switch between them quickly.</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="getting-started">
<title>Getting Started</title>

<sect1 id="adding-server">
<title>Adding a Server</title>
<para>When &i18n-kapplication; is started for the first time, you are asked to add
a server account. You can add other accounts later with
<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Add Server…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.
Enter the server &URL; and choose an authentication method.</para>

<para>Depending on what the server allows, the following authentication methods are
available:</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>User name (or email) and password</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Personal access token</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>OAuth providers such as Google, GitHub, GitLab, Facebook or Twitter</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>

<para>If two-factor authentication is enabled on your account, &i18n-kapplication;
asks for the code when you log in. Passwords are stored in the system wallet.</para>

<para>If the server allows it, you can create a new account with
<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Register a New User…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="multiple-servers">
<title>Using Several Servers</title>
<para>Each configured account appears as a tab. Use
<menuchoice><guimenu>Window</guimenu><guimenuitem>Next Server</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and
<menuchoice><guimenu>Window</guimenu><guimenuitem>Previous Server</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
to switch between them. Accounts can be enabled, disabled, reordered or removed in the
<guilabel>Accounts</guilabel> page of the settings dialog.</para>

<para><menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Export Accounts</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
and <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Import Accounts</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
let you move your account configuration to another computer.</para>
</sect1>
</chapter>

<chapter id="main-window">
<title>The Main Window</title>

<sect1 id="room-list">
<title>The Room List</title>
<para>The left side of the window lists your channels, private groups, direct messages,
discussions and teams. A search field at the top filters the list. Your status
(online, busy, away, offline, or a custom status) can be changed from the status bar
at the bottom of the window.</para>

<para>The <guimenu>View</guimenu> menu changes how the list looks:</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><guimenuitem>Condensed</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Medium</guimenuitem> or
<guimenuitem>Extended</guimenuitem> display</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Sorting <guimenuitem>By Last Message</guimenuitem> or
<guimenuitem>Alphabetically</guimenuitem>, with optional <guimenuitem>Unread on Top</guimenuitem></para></listitem>
<listitem><para><guimenuitem>Show Room Avatar</guimenuitem> and
<guimenuitem>Show Favorite Room</guimenuitem></para></listitem>
<listitem><para><guimenuitem>Mark All Channels as Read</guimenuitem></para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>

<para><menuchoice><guimenu>Channel</guimenu><guimenuitem>Jump to Next Unread Channel</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
takes you to the next room with unread messages.</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="room-view">
<title>The Room View</title>
<para>The right side of the window shows the messages of the selected room. The header
displays the room name and topic, and contains buttons to mark the room as favorite,
open the room information, list its users, search messages, start a call, and open
the room menu.</para>

<para>The room menu gives access to:</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Pinned, starred and mentioned messages, threads, discussions and file attachments</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Adding or inviting users, showing banned users</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Notification settings for this room</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Automatic translation of messages</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Exporting or pruning messages (with the required permissions)</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>End-to-end encryption, when the server supports it</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</sect1>
</chapter>

<chapter id="messages">
<title>Messages</title>

<sect1 id="writing-messages">
<title>Writing Messages</title>
<para>Type your message in the text field at the bottom of the room and press &Enter;
to send it. Messages support Markdown formatting. Typing <literal>@</literal> completes
user names, <literal>#</literal> completes channel names, <literal>:</literal> completes
emoji and <literal>/</literal> lists the slash commands available on the server.</para>

<para>The buttons next to the text field let you:</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Insert an emoji, including the custom emoji of the server</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Attach one or more files (you can also drag and drop or paste them)</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Record and send a sound message or a video message</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Use the tools provided by plugins, such as taking a screenshot</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>

<para>Spell checking and auto-correction are available while typing and can be configured
in the settings dialog.</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="message-actions">
<title>Acting on Messages</title>
<para>Hovering a message shows buttons to add a reaction, reply in a thread or star the
message. Its context menu offers more actions, depending on your permissions:</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Edit, delete or quote the message</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Copy the message, the selection, or a link to the message</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Reply in a thread, follow or unfollow it, show the full thread</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Start a discussion or a private conversation from the message</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Pin, star, forward or report the message</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Mark the message as unread</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Translate the message, or show the original text</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Show read receipts, when enabled on the server</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>

<para>Images, videos and sounds are displayed inline and can be opened in a viewer.
&URL; previews can be enabled in the settings.</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="searching">
<title>Searching</title>
<para>Use the search button of the room header to search the messages of the current room.
<menuchoice><guimenu>Channel</guimenu><guimenuitem>Join Room…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>,
<guimenuitem>Join Team…</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Open Private Conversation…</guimenuitem>
search the server directory for rooms, teams and users.</para>
</sect1>
</chapter>

<chapter id="rooms">
<title>Rooms, Discussions and Teams</title>
<para>The <guimenu>Channel</guimenu> menu lets you create:</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><guimenuitem>Create New Channel…</guimenuitem>: a public channel or a private group,
optionally read-only, broadcast or encrypted</para></listitem>
<listitem><para><guimenuitem>Create Direct Messages…</guimenuitem>: a conversation with one or more users</para></listitem>
<listitem><para><guimenuitem>Create Discussion…</guimenuitem>: a sub-conversation attached to a room</para></listitem>
<listitem><para><guimenuitem>Create Team…</guimenuitem>: a group of users with its own channels</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>

<para>The room information dialog shows the name, topic, announcement, description and
avatar of the room. Owners can edit them, change the room type, set a password, and
configure options such as read-only mode or message pruning. Team owners can add,
remove and convert team channels.</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="notifications">
<title>Notifications</title>
<para>&i18n-kapplication; uses the desktop notification system to tell you about new
messages and mentions, and shows unread counters in the room list and in the system tray.
Notification behavior (desktop alert, sound, email) can be set for each room with
<guimenuitem>Configure Notification…</guimenuitem> in the room menu.</para>

<para><menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Notify History</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
lists the notifications you received during the session.</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="encryption">
<title>End-to-End Encryption</title>
<para>When the server enables it, &i18n-kapplication; supports Rocket.Chat end-to-end
encryption for direct messages and private groups. Your encryption keys are protected
by a password that you can manage in the <guilabel>Encryption</guilabel> page of
<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>My Account…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.
Encrypted rooms show a lock icon in their header. Note that the content of encrypted
messages cannot be searched.</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="my-account">
<title>My Account</title>
<para><menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>My Account…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
lets you manage your Rocket.Chat profile:</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Profile: name, user name, email, avatar, status message and password</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Preferences offered by the server</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Two-factor authentication (email or TOTP)</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>End-to-end encryption keys</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Personal access tokens</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Devices logged in to your account</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Feature previews</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</chapter>

<chapter id="administration">
<title>Server Administration</title>
<para>Users with the required permissions can administer the server from
<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Administration</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.</para>

<para><guimenuitem>Administrator…</guimenuitem> gives access to server information, rooms,
users, invites, custom emoji, custom sounds, custom user statuses, roles, permissions,
OAuth applications, the moderation console and the server logs.</para>

<para><guimenuitem>Server Settings…</guimenuitem> lets you change the server configuration,
and the <guimenuitem>Applications</guimenuitem> entries let you browse and manage
Rocket.Chat Marketplace applications.</para>

<para><menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Server Checklist…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
checks the server configuration for common problems.</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="offline">
<title>Offline Mode</title>
<para>&i18n-kapplication; can keep messages in a local database (enable
<guilabel>Enable local database</guilabel> in the <guilabel>General</guilabel> settings),
so that rooms are displayed faster and remain readable when the connection is lost.
<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Work Offline</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
disconnects from the server on purpose.</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="configuration">
<title>Configuring &i18n-kapplication;</title>
<para><menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &i18n-kapplication;…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
opens the settings dialog, which contains the following pages:</para>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry><term><guilabel>Accounts</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Add, modify, enable, disable or remove server accounts.</para></listitem></varlistentry>
<varlistentry><term><guilabel>General</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>System tray icon, status on startup, image and &URL; previews, animated GIFs,
local database, logging, and other behavior options.</para></listitem></varlistentry>
<varlistentry><term><guilabel>Font</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Font used to display messages.</para></listitem></varlistentry>
<varlistentry><term><guilabel>Spell Checking</guilabel> and <guilabel>Auto-Correction</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Language and correction rules used while typing.</para></listitem></varlistentry>
<varlistentry><term><guilabel>Translation</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Translation engine used to translate messages.</para></listitem></varlistentry>
<varlistentry><term><guilabel>Accessibility</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Text-to-speech and speech-to-text options, when available.</para></listitem></varlistentry>
<varlistentry><term><guilabel>Plugins</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Enable or disable plugins, for example sharing text, web shortcuts,
screenshots, or text generation with an AI engine.</para></listitem></varlistentry>
<varlistentry><term><guilabel>User Feedback</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Choose which anonymous usage statistics are sent to the developers.</para></listitem></varlistentry>
</variablelist>
<para>The color scheme can be changed in the <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu, and the
message font size in the <guimenu>View</guimenu> menu.</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="tools">
<title>Tools</title>
<para>The <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> menu provides helpers mostly useful for troubleshooting:</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><guimenuitem>Show Channel Log</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Show Server Errors</guimenuitem></para></listitem>
<listitem><para><guimenuitem>Show RocketChat Information</guimenuitem>: version and capabilities of the server</para></listitem>
<listitem><para><guimenuitem>Retry Wallet Access</guimenuitem>, when the password could not be read from the wallet</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</chapter>

